# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ClassroomLens Pro — Environment Variables
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# STEP 1: Copy this file and rename it to .env
#         (just remove the .example)
#
# STEP 2: Save the file and run: npm run dev
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Anthropic (Claude API) — SERVER-SIDE only, used by /api/claude.
#
# Deliberately NOT prefixed VITE_ — that prefix makes Vite inline a
# variable's value into the public JS bundle at build time. The whole
# point of routing Claude calls through /api/claude is that this key
# never reaches the browser, so it must never carry that prefix.
# Get a key at https://console.anthropic.com and set it in Vercel:
# Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables. Only takes effect once
# deployed (or via `vercel dev` locally) — plain `npm run dev` does not
# run the /api functions at all.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase (accounts + cloud storage)
#
# STEP 1: Create a free project at https://supabase.com
# STEP 2: Go to Settings -> API in your project dashboard
# STEP 3: Copy the "Project URL" and "anon public" key below
#         (the anon key is safe to expose in frontend code —
#         do NOT use the service_role key here)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key-goes-here

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Stripe billing (Monthly / Annual flat-rate plans — no free trial,
# no metering)
#
# These are SERVER-SIDE variables for the /api serverless functions —
# they do NOT go in this .env file and must never have a VITE_ prefix
# (that prefix makes a variable part of the public frontend bundle).
# Set them in Vercel: Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
# They only take effect once deployed (or via `vercel dev` locally) —
# plain `npm run dev` does not run the /api functions at all.
#
# STEP 1: Create a Stripe account at https://dashboard.stripe.com and
#         stay in Test mode while setting this up.
# STEP 2: Dashboard → Developers → API keys → copy the Secret key.
# STEP 3: Dashboard → Product catalog → create one Product with two
#         recurring Prices:
#           - $9.99/month  -> STRIPE_PRICE_MONTHLY
#           - $59.99/year  -> STRIPE_PRICE_ANNUAL
# STEP 4: Supabase Dashboard → Settings → API → copy the
#         service_role key (NOT the anon key) for SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY.
# STEP 5: Webhook — after your first deploy, Dashboard → Developers →
#         Webhooks → Add endpoint → https://your-app.vercel.app/api/stripe-webhook
#         Listen for: checkout.session.completed, invoice.paid,
#         invoice.payment_failed, customer.subscription.deleted.
#         Copy the resulting signing secret into STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET.
#         (checkout.session.completed is also verified directly via the
#         Stripe API on the success redirect — see
#         api/verify-checkout-session.js — the webhook remains the
#         authoritative record and the only path for renewals/cancellations.)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
# SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key-goes-here
# STRIPE_PRICE_MONTHLY=price_...
# STRIPE_PRICE_ANNUAL=price_...
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# IMPORTANT: Never share your .env file or commit it to GitHub.
# The .gitignore file already excludes it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
